{"tool_name":"chemgps-np","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"chemgps-np","home":"http://chemgps.bmc.uu.se/","summary":"A tool tuned for navigation in biologically relevant chemical space.","addition_date":"2015-12-07T13:00:03Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:58:52Z","tool_type":["Web API","Web application","Web service"],"version":["1"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:chemgps-np","credit":[{"email":"chemgps@bmc.uu.se","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"bils.se","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://chemgps.bmc.uu.se/batchelor/about.php"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Molecular property","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2087"}}],"operation":[{"term":"Analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2945"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Molecular property","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2087"}}]}],"name":"ChemGPS-NP","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"mikael.borg@bils.se","publication":[{"doi":"10.1007/s10822-008-9255-y","metadata":{"abstract":"Internet has become a central source for information, tools, and services facilitating the work for medicinal chemists and drug discoverers worldwide. In this paper we introduce a web-based public tool, ChemGPS-NPWeb (http://chemgps.bmc.uu.se), for comprehensive chemical space navigation and exploration in terms of global mapping onto a consistent, eight dimensional map over structure derived physico-chemical characteristics. ChemGPS-NPWeb can assist in compound selection and prioritization; property description and interpretation; cluster analysis and neighbourhood mapping; as well as comparison and characterization of large compound datasets. By using ChemGPS-NPWeb, researchers can analyze and compare chemical libraries in a consistent manner. In this study it is demonstrated how ChemGPS-NPWeb can assist in interpreting 